    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='XML External Entities and Template Injection',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains X X E and Template Injection, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] First, a simple definition. [[slnc 300]] An X M L parser and a template engine both run instructions found in their input, so an invoice upload can read the server\'s files and a customer\'s name can run inside an e-mail template, unless the parser refuses a DOCTYPE and the engine has no expressions. [[slnc 600]] Think of it this way. [[slnc 300]] Think of an assistant who types up whatever a letter says to do. A letter that says "enclose a copy of the file in the top drawer" gets the file enclosed, and a form letter whose blanks are filled by the customer can be made to say "and read out the safe\'s code". The fix is an assistant who types up the letter and does not follow it, and a form that has blanks only for names. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online store. [[slnc 500]] By the end, you will be able to: [[slnc 300]] Explain what a DOCTYPE and an external entity are, and what the parser does with them. [[slnc 300]] List the parser settings that stop X X E and say why refusing the DOCTYPE comes first. [[slnc 300]] Explain why customer text must never become part of a template.'),
